.TH "CSDLC-CUTOVER" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-cutover \- apply an explicitly authorized authority transition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc cutover 505 \-\-operation OPERATION.json [\-\-execute]
\&csdlc cutover \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
\&csdlc cutover \-\-help
.fi
.SH ISSUE INTENT FORM
\&The semantic issue intent form is the current operational interface. It resolves the authenticated repository and issue context, reserves the administrative semantic operation before any effect and retains the exact native outcome.
.PP
\&OPERATION.json is a complete TerminalRouteRequest whose cutover.operation is apply. Its repository, issue 505, primary repository root and nested cutover.execute value must exactly match the semantic invocation. \-\-execute is required for mutation; omission produces a read\-only preflight.
.PP
\&Optional \-\-repo\-root selects discovery, \-\-json retains machine output, and \-\-emit\-request returns a generated wrapper accepted directly by COMMAND \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json; its inner request is also accepted. Both forms share identity, approval and mutation guards.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax and \-\-observe\-github flag are retired. They remain visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current administrative interface.
.PP
\&Retained authority\-transition owner for an explicitly operator\-reviewed cutover. It requires cutover approval, source provenance, rollback evidence, undo boundary and authenticated #505 evidence. Historical approval cannot authorize a new transition.
.SH OPTIONS
\&\-\-operation: Required path to explicit operation content. The owner derives repository and issue identity from the semantic context.
.PP
\&\-\-execute: Request the guarded administrative effect. Omit it for read\-only preview.
.PP
\&\-\-intent\-request: Execute an exact generated csdlc.v3.intent_request.v1 request or its generated wrapper; stale snapshots fail closed.
.PP
\&\-\-repo\-root: Select repository discovery; it cannot override bound issue identity.
.PP
\&\-\-json: Retain machine\-readable JSON output.
.PP
\&\-\-emit\-request: Emit the generated semantic request without executing it.
.PP
\&\-\-request: Retired direct\-writer input retained only for migration discovery.
.PP
\&\-\-observe\-github: Retired direct\-writer flag retained only for migration discovery.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.SH OPERATION
\&TerminalRouteRequest with cutover.operation apply. The semantic adapter requires issue 505 and exact repository, repository\-root and execute identity before the terminal owner is called. See csdlc\-requests(1).
.SH EFFECTS
\&Preview is read\-only. An admitted \-\-execute invocation may replace the selected binary or authority selector and retain the guarded transition receipt; proof and preview do not authorize execution.
.SH FILES
\&Primary terminal paths use resolved Git metadata under csdlc\-v3/local/v3/issues/505 and csdlc\-v3/local/evidence/505. Linked paths remain under .csdlc. The operation repository root must be the exact primary reconciliation checkout.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax and \-\-observe\-github flag are retired. They remain visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current administrative interface.
.nf
\&csdlc cutover 505 \-\-operation cutover\-operation.json
\&csdlc cutover 505 \-\-operation cutover\-operation.json \-\-execute
.fi
.PP
\&Examples validate syntax and the denial boundary; they do not grant transition authorization.
.SH RECOVERY
\&Retain the original operation and exact checkout identity. A pending administrative transaction is reconciled from its retained canonical request; caller replacement bytes are not accepted. Unsupported or unproven state fails closed.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1).
